00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.750
And so I'm sure you can
name right along with me

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.090
everything that crossed my mind,

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.640
and Jackie already pointed
to many of those things,

00:14:54.665 --> 00:14:57.370
the ongoing dishonoring
of Breonna Taylor's life.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.600
The fact that our president

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:01.115
or the president of the United States

00:15:01.115 --> 00:15:03.633
sent out of clarion call
for white supremacists

00:15:03.633 --> 00:15:04.883
on national TV blatantly.

00:15:06.009 --> 00:15:07.790
The generations long
trajectory of the Supreme Court

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.510
upon the death of Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.610
As you all know all too well,
the gutting of voting rights

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:16.890
and our civil liberties, and
the many, many, many, many,

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.650
many, too many ways to name
that black life has been

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.480
and continues to be snatched.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.460
The pandemic, state sanctioned murder,

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.880
withholding of life saving resources,

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.493
environmental devastation.

00:15:30.672 --> 00:15:31.505
This is where I started to name,

00:15:31.505 --> 00:15:34.610
this is where I started to
start and then I stopped

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:39.060
because I believe we have
to make our arms wider,

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.070
we have to hold a different
type of space simultaneously,

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.030
we have to claim something different.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:46.580
We have to claim those
combinations of forces

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:49.300
and histories that allow
you and I to even be here

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:50.583
in conversation today.

00:15:52.006 --> 00:15:53.680
We have to name for whom
we are holding this space

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.300
and who is holding us in this space,

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.170
this is where we have to start now.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.760
So we will, of course, we
will address all the things,

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:04.750
all the things, we will talk
about what we are up against,

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.280
we will talk about black
voters matter and suppression

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:10.210
and resistance in the face of everything

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.010
that we are struggling through and with.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:15.640
But I wanna open this space

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:19.610
from a place that reminds
us of our inheritance,

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:23.370
our inheritance of strength,
fierce intellect, courage,

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:28.070
innovation, community
care and of course love.

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:30.150
This is where we want to end up,

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:31.703
this is where we have to start.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.660
So I want to call into this
space, into our conversation,

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:40.390
two people that I know we both
hold dear, our mutual friend

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.550
and fierce advocate for
black women and girls,

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:45.703
Tynesha McHarris and Angela Davis.

00:16:47.074 --> 00:16:48.394
- Ashay, ashay.

00:16:48.394 --> 00:16:49.227
- Hmm.

00:16:49.227 --> 00:16:52.980
Tynesha says, "My power and my humanity

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:56.190
are not experienced through who I control

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:58.713
but through who I love
and am accountable to.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:01.480
My power and my humanity

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.690
are not experienced through who I control

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.997
but through who I love
and am accountable to."

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.757
Angela Davis, a little bit longer,

00:17:10.757 --> 00:17:12.510
"The work of the political activist

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.550
inevitably involved a certain tension

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.400
between the requirements
that positions be taken

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.960
on current issues as they arise

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:22.510
and the desire that one's contributions

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.483
will somehow survive the ravages of time.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.600
In this sense, the most
difficult challenge

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:32.730
facing the activist is to respond fully

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:36.510
to the needs of the moment
and to do so in such a way

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:39.700
that the light one attempts
to shine on the present

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.980
simultaneously illuminates the future."

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:45.078
- Hmm, powerful.
So, LaTosha,

00:17:45.078 --> 00:17:47.920
these words remind me of
my first vision of you,

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:50.560
which is that of a traveler,

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.580
and so let me explain what I mean by that.

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:54.240
I feel that you are rooted and nurtured

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.330
by the lessons of the past,
the work and blueprint

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.720
etched in our very spirits

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.960
by those who breathed air
on this troubled Earth

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.980
long, long before us.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:06.400
Your work at the same time
sit squarely and resolutely

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:10.900
in the urgency of the now
as you mobilize all of this

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.670
with a prophetic imagination

00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:15.710
that is gazing towards our black futures

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.650
and you know there is no real distinction

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:19.600
between these three planes.

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:22.830
You show us so clearly how to
live in all of them at once,

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.130
how to do work in all of them at once

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:28.240
guided by the fierce undeterred
love for black communities

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:31.290
that Tynesha talks about
that as a source of light

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:34.460
that illuminates how you
manifest accountability

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.363
in your political,
intellectual and activist work.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:41.800
So I honor you and I wanna
start with that grounding,

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:45.420
with those roots, black
voters matter is necessary

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:47.180
for all of the reasons we will get into

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:50.640
but I would love for you to
situate black voters matter

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.280
in a larger history because I
want people to understand that

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:57.640
as powerful as the work is, it
is part of a broader strategy

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.610
for manifesting black
political power, right?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.250
And let me be clear, not empire building,

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.990
but black political power
and so we know that voting

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.080
is in this moment, especially,
so that we can come up

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:12.230
and fight another day,
live to fight another day,

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:16.230
but I want you to talk about
how you see Black Voters Matter

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:19.730
as part of this longer political project

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:20.930
that you've been involved in

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.090
for decades and decades and decades.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.470
And lastly I'll just say,
how you see black women,

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.580
the mobilization of black
women and your relationships

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.670
with intergenerational
groups of black women

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.320
being a part of this foundation.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.871
- Hmm.

00:19:35.871 --> 00:19:40.871
