01:10:41.570 --> 01:10:42.860
what should we be focused on,

01:10:42.860 --> 01:10:44.500
what should our eyes be focused on?

01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:47.463
Where should our actions be rooted now?

01:10:51.488 --> 01:10:53.360
- So just to kind of even build off

01:10:53.360 --> 01:10:54.570
even from your last question,

01:10:54.570 --> 01:10:57.410
what I wanted to get to is
that at the end of the day,

01:10:57.410 --> 01:11:02.410
Dr. King said it, I've
struggled whether I,

01:11:02.680 --> 01:11:05.980
particularly a sizable
amount of my adulthood,

01:11:05.980 --> 01:11:08.613
whether I believe it or
not, I know it to be true.

01:11:10.950 --> 01:11:13.960
Love is the only force
that's greater than hate.

01:11:13.960 --> 01:11:15.530
I know that to be true.

01:11:15.530 --> 01:11:17.550
And so in that what drives me

01:11:17.550 --> 01:11:21.220
and drives the millions of
other folks that we work with,

01:11:21.220 --> 01:11:24.550
that are actually doing the
work on the ground is love

01:11:24.550 --> 01:11:27.320
and our collective power.

01:11:27.320 --> 01:11:29.260
So some of the things that we're doing

01:11:29.260 --> 01:11:31.230
even at the polling sites, we've seen it,

01:11:31.230 --> 01:11:33.910
'cause oftentimes those same
folks like the Proud Boys,

01:11:33.910 --> 01:11:37.080
they're cowards, they're not
used to being challenged,

01:11:37.080 --> 01:11:38.490
they're not used to really being able

01:11:38.490 --> 01:11:40.640
to come up against collective power,

01:11:40.640 --> 01:11:44.120
they're not used to really
being able to be accountable.

01:11:44.120 --> 01:11:46.290
And so oftentimes I
think what we have to do

01:11:46.290 --> 01:11:48.460
is we have to show our forces

01:11:48.460 --> 01:11:50.740
and show up collectively together,

01:11:50.740 --> 01:11:52.020
that's the best way to do it.

01:11:52.020 --> 01:11:55.500
So I am encouraging folks,
this is part of our,

01:11:55.500 --> 01:12:00.190
there was a great question
earlier around whether people,

01:12:00.190 --> 01:12:02.717
I'm not one of the ones that I think,

01:12:09.942 --> 01:12:14.942
I think that we are not
the, you know, I believe,

01:12:16.375 --> 01:12:20.020
oh, I forgot my thought,
the bottom line is that

01:12:20.020 --> 01:12:22.300
people are showing up at,

01:12:22.300 --> 01:12:25.300
we've got to show up at the poling site.

01:12:25.300 --> 01:12:29.100
We've got to say that we
are standing in our power.

01:12:29.100 --> 01:12:32.760
The whole purpose of our
We Got Power campaign

01:12:32.760 --> 01:12:34.780
is to say that we've got power.

01:12:34.780 --> 01:12:38.800
Love is our power, our
resiliency is our power

01:12:38.800 --> 01:12:41.280
and I'm not one of those
folks that believe that

01:12:41.280 --> 01:12:43.140
we don't have the right to bear arms.

01:12:43.140 --> 01:12:44.510
I know I'm not one of those people

01:12:44.510 --> 01:12:48.760
that believe that folks of color

01:12:48.760 --> 01:12:51.020
should not have protection for themselves.

01:12:51.020 --> 01:12:53.960
I will say this though, I
think when we get to the space

01:12:53.960 --> 01:12:57.250
that we get in the game of
violence meets violence,

01:12:57.250 --> 01:12:58.660
I mean, what are we gonna
do, have a shootout?

01:12:58.660 --> 01:12:59.910
I mean, you know what I'm saying?

01:12:59.910 --> 01:13:02.810
Like where's the ending sight on that.

01:13:02.810 --> 01:13:05.700
And so I think we have to
strategically recognize

01:13:05.700 --> 01:13:07.810
that part of what happens
and even with Trump,

01:13:07.810 --> 01:13:09.720
when he's really challenged on it,

01:13:09.720 --> 01:13:11.430
he talks mad trash when he by himself

01:13:11.430 --> 01:13:13.653
and when he's around his
crew but he ain't said that

01:13:13.653 --> 01:13:17.360
in a black community yet
about the Proud Boys, right?

01:13:17.360 --> 01:13:19.600
My point, because there's
an element of racist

01:13:19.600 --> 01:13:22.790
that literally there's
a space of cowardice.

01:13:22.790 --> 01:13:25.110
And so what we've seen and experienced

01:13:25.110 --> 01:13:27.710
that just having people
at the polling sites,

01:13:27.710 --> 01:13:30.400
just having poll workers and poll watchers

01:13:30.400 --> 01:13:32.510
that are trained at the polling sites,

01:13:32.510 --> 01:13:36.190
that just having people that
are there, that bear witness,

01:13:36.190 --> 01:13:37.940
I can tell you, it makes a difference.

01:13:37.940 --> 01:13:40.560
It makes a difference how
the people on the inside act,

01:13:40.560 --> 01:13:43.600
it makes a difference on how
the people on the outside act,

01:13:43.600 --> 01:13:46.225
that in some ways what you've got to do

01:13:46.225 --> 01:13:48.658
is you've got to really be
able to go to the process,

01:13:48.658 --> 01:13:51.750
be driven not by hate and
fear but be driven by love.

01:13:51.750 --> 01:13:53.000
That we love our community

01:13:53.000 --> 01:13:54.910
to the extent that we're
gonna protect our community,

01:13:54.910 --> 01:13:56.750
that we're going to fight for democracy,

01:13:56.750 --> 01:13:59.730
that we're literally going
to do everything in our power

01:13:59.730 --> 01:14:01.100
to engage folks.

01:14:01.100 --> 01:14:06.100
The fact that right now
there are children in cages

01:14:06.670 --> 01:14:10.440
because they've got a
different color passport,

01:14:10.440 --> 01:14:12.440
what is wrong with us?

01:14:12.440 --> 01:14:14.680
The fact that there were women

01:14:14.680 --> 01:14:16.960
who had forced hysterectomies

01:14:18.219 --> 01:14:20.260
and are not able to bear children

01:14:20.260 --> 01:14:23.570
because they were seeking
refuge in this country

01:14:23.570 --> 01:14:26.850
for us to dare to brag on some way

01:14:26.850 --> 01:14:29.790
that fundamentally America is the greatest

01:14:30.880 --> 01:14:32.820
yet we would do that to other human beings

01:14:32.820 --> 01:14:34.340
because of what, passport.

01:14:34.340 --> 01:14:36.940
If you ain't mad and pissed
off, something is wrong.

01:14:38.870 --> 01:14:40.700
We are literally in this space

01:14:40.700 --> 01:14:42.300
that we've got a president office,

01:14:42.300 --> 01:14:44.480
I don't care about his economic policy,

01:14:44.480 --> 01:14:46.280
I don't care about any of his policy,

01:14:46.280 --> 01:14:50.530
the fact that he would use
hate as a vehicle to organize

01:14:50.530 --> 01:14:54.350
and keep himself in power,
that's all I need to know.

01:14:54.350 --> 01:14:57.180
I'm raising this because we keep operating

01:14:57.180 --> 01:15:00.093
as if this is just some
different political election

01:15:00.093 --> 01:15:02.690
that oh, it's the Democrat
or the Republicans,

01:15:02.690 --> 01:15:04.990
I don't need to hear
another debate, for what?

01:15:06.730 --> 01:15:08.600
Fundamentally we know what's at stake

01:15:08.600 --> 01:15:11.650
and fundamentally we're
going to have to connect

01:15:11.650 --> 01:15:13.170
on how it's gonna be different.

01:15:13.170 --> 01:15:15.520
And I do wanna do, I
wanna do something, Aimee,

01:15:15.520 --> 01:15:17.040
if it's possible with everybody

01:15:17.040 --> 01:15:18.830
that's on this call right now.

01:15:18.830 --> 01:15:20.890
I'm just gonna ask you all
if you can just get centered,

01:15:20.890 --> 01:15:22.980
I do this all the time, I just
want you all to get centered

01:15:22.980 --> 01:15:25.830
wherever you are, just kind
of get centered and grounded.

01:15:29.870 --> 01:15:32.033
I'm gonna ask you to close your eyes.

01:15:36.850 --> 01:15:38.300
I'm gonna ask you a question.

01:15:39.458 --> 01:15:40.291
Keep your eyes closed.

01:15:45.380 --> 01:15:48.123
Imagine America without racism.

01:15:58.909 --> 01:15:59.980
And I know we don't have much time

01:15:59.980 --> 01:16:02.580
so I'm gonna ask you to go
ahead and open your eyes.

01:16:04.790 --> 01:16:06.903
How many of you could
actually see something?

01:16:09.140 --> 01:16:12.970
I do this exercise all over the place.

01:16:12.970 --> 01:16:15.790
I do it at Harvard, I
do it in the community,

01:16:15.790 --> 01:16:18.780
I did it on a basketball court last night.

01:16:18.780 --> 01:16:23.780
Time and time again 99.9% most of the time

01:16:24.156 --> 01:16:25.720
of the people that I ask that question

01:16:25.720 --> 01:16:29.260
can't even imagine this
country without racism.

01:16:29.260 --> 01:16:33.060
And so my next question to
you is what has been created

01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:35.880
and brought into being
in the physical world

01:16:35.880 --> 01:16:38.150
that wasn't first envisioned?

01:16:38.150 --> 01:16:39.630
This cell phone,

01:16:39.630 --> 01:16:42.890
somebody actually had
the see the cell phone

01:16:42.890 --> 01:16:44.490
for it to be created.

01:16:44.490 --> 01:16:47.200
Someone had to see this
microphone for it to be created.

01:16:47.200 --> 01:16:49.020
There is nothing, look around your room,

01:16:49.020 --> 01:16:51.460
there's nothing that is in existence

01:16:51.460 --> 01:16:54.720
that someone did not envision at first.

01:16:54.720 --> 01:16:58.480
I'm raising this because
if we do not shift

01:16:58.480 --> 01:17:01.530
and move past just responding to what is

01:17:01.530 --> 01:17:02.930
and envision something different,

01:17:02.930 --> 01:17:04.040
we will never achieve it

01:17:04.040 --> 01:17:08.877
because we can't bring that
into being which we do not.

01:17:25.572 --> 01:17:28.458
- LaTosha, can you hear me?

01:17:28.458 --> 01:17:32.875
- I know I'm breaking, if
you all can close your eyes

01:17:34.750 --> 01:17:39.750
my question is what is
your radical re-imagining

01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:42.073
of this nation?

01:17:47.190 --> 01:17:48.343
Open your eyes.

01:17:50.380 --> 01:17:53.493
That's where we've got
to spend more time y'all.

01:17:54.940 --> 01:17:58.600
That's where we've got to spend more time.

01:17:58.600 --> 01:18:02.340
We will constantly continue
to be in this rat race

01:18:02.340 --> 01:18:04.000
and this hamster wheel

01:18:04.000 --> 01:18:07.890
of having the same regenerated
conversations about racism

01:18:09.052 --> 01:18:12.690
until we can actually hold
something different in our minds

01:18:12.690 --> 01:18:15.820
that we want to actually
bring into the world.

01:18:15.820 --> 01:18:19.230
When I talk about, oftentimes
I tell folks around

01:18:19.230 --> 01:18:21.310
what is it that we can't reimagine.

01:18:21.310 --> 01:18:23.960
That at the end of the day, I
even think about the workweek.

01:18:23.960 --> 01:18:25.560
Has anybody ever thought about,

01:18:25.560 --> 01:18:27.710
like what's the magic of 40 hours a week?

01:18:27.710 --> 01:18:29.130
Like what's the magic of that?

01:18:29.130 --> 01:18:31.490
If technology is created so

01:18:31.490 --> 01:18:33.740
that it actually cuts down production,

01:18:33.740 --> 01:18:35.470
why are we not passing on

01:18:35.470 --> 01:18:39.010
the benefits of the means of
production down to the workers?

01:18:39.010 --> 01:18:42.500
Why couldn't we, if it
used to take 1,000 workers

01:18:42.500 --> 01:18:45.910
to make 100 cars and now
it only takes 10 workers,

01:18:45.910 --> 01:18:48.080
I mean, 10 hours to make 100 cars,

01:18:48.080 --> 01:18:51.320
why don't we keep all the
workers, cut down their time

01:18:51.320 --> 01:18:52.790
and actually give them more money?

01:18:52.790 --> 01:18:54.610
That is possible.

01:18:54.610 --> 01:18:55.930
We could use technology

01:18:55.930 --> 01:19:00.670
where people could work 15
hours a week and make more money

01:19:00.670 --> 01:19:03.390
and spend time with their
family and their children.

01:19:03.390 --> 01:19:06.723
Most of us until COVID-19
didn't even know our kids.

01:19:08.150 --> 01:19:11.433
We know 'em on the weekend
but we didn't see 'em.

01:19:11.433 --> 01:19:13.280
They were being raised by a system

01:19:13.280 --> 01:19:15.250
that fundamentally is even telling them

01:19:15.250 --> 01:19:17.020
oftentimes that they're inferior.

01:19:17.020 --> 01:19:19.770
Why can't we reimagine education?

01:19:19.770 --> 01:19:22.890
Why can't we reimagine every
single system in this country,

01:19:22.890 --> 01:19:24.310
that the economy is not based on

01:19:24.310 --> 01:19:26.530
how well the stock market is doing

01:19:26.530 --> 01:19:29.370
but how well her people
are doing in this country?

01:19:29.370 --> 01:19:31.730
But it will never get there

01:19:31.730 --> 01:19:36.070
if we don't radically
reimagine every single system.

01:19:36.070 --> 01:19:39.590
And so I can come and talk
about all my challenges

01:19:39.590 --> 01:19:41.400
about America and its system.

01:19:41.400 --> 01:19:43.640
I can come and talk about what
we need to do in the moment

01:19:43.640 --> 01:19:46.150
because this is what we
have right now and so,

01:19:46.150 --> 01:19:51.150
but I also have to think of
myself as a black futurist.

01:19:51.190 --> 01:19:54.830
I don't have the luxury just
to respond to what is now,

01:19:54.830 --> 01:19:58.630
that while I am responding
to what is now, I am off

01:19:58.630 --> 01:20:02.550
and pushing my mind to
think about what is possible

01:20:02.550 --> 01:20:05.010
because I want to bring it into being

01:20:05.010 --> 01:20:08.530
just like Steve Jobs wanted to
bring this iPhone into being,

01:20:08.530 --> 01:20:13.530
but it will never happen
if we're not spending time,

01:20:13.730 --> 01:20:17.300
not just fighting what is
but creating some space

01:20:17.300 --> 01:20:18.390
for us to reimagine.

01:20:18.390 --> 01:20:21.210
And so with this, I'll stop.

01:20:21.210 --> 01:20:23.630
I'll just say that with this
it's important for us to know

01:20:23.630 --> 01:20:25.480
that what's at stake right now,

01:20:25.480 --> 01:20:27.470
that oftentimes sometimes we have to make

01:20:27.470 --> 01:20:30.560
a tactical decision around
voting that we just give people,

01:20:30.560 --> 01:20:34.020
buy them a little space, just
a little grace and space.

01:20:34.020 --> 01:20:36.350
They may not be able, that
person that's in office

01:20:36.350 --> 01:20:38.850
might not be the person
that's gonna be the person

01:20:38.850 --> 01:20:41.020
that we need to make a
transformative change,

01:20:41.020 --> 01:20:44.350
they may just be the transitional
person and that's okay

01:20:44.350 --> 01:20:48.000
but every single thing
that's available to us,

01:20:48.000 --> 01:20:49.370
every single tool.

01:20:49.370 --> 01:20:53.650
I love my community and
I love humanity so much

01:20:53.650 --> 01:20:56.390
that every single tool that is available,

01:20:56.390 --> 01:20:58.380
that is within my reach to use,

01:20:58.380 --> 01:21:00.870
I am actively trying to think

01:21:00.870 --> 01:21:04.970
how can I use that to provide some space

01:21:04.970 --> 01:21:08.810
for people to create that which
I want to see in the world.

01:21:08.810 --> 01:21:10.630
And so we've got to also see

01:21:10.630 --> 01:21:13.900
this as what we're doing in the meantime

01:21:13.900 --> 01:21:17.033
is I see it as a boat
that you're on a big boat,

01:21:18.492 --> 01:21:20.420
you're on the Titanic out in the water

01:21:20.420 --> 01:21:21.750
and the Titanic is sinking

01:21:21.750 --> 01:21:24.713
and all you got is this
little raggedy lifeboat.

01:21:27.378 --> 01:21:28.650
That's all you got, that's all you got

01:21:29.890 --> 01:21:33.100
but the goal is I got
to make it to the shore

01:21:33.100 --> 01:21:35.870
so that I can get to the shore
and I can create that boat

01:21:35.870 --> 01:21:39.100
which I know that I
deserved in my communities.

01:21:39.100 --> 01:21:42.080
And so we've got to really
be able to be tactical

01:21:42.080 --> 01:21:45.803
in how we see elections in
a way that we're not seeing,

01:21:47.050 --> 01:21:48.893
do we have the perfect candidate?

01:21:51.000 --> 01:21:54.040
We've got to see it around what decision,

01:21:54.040 --> 01:21:55.940
'cause a decision is gonna be made,

01:21:55.940 --> 01:21:58.340
that is going to create
the least amount of harm

01:21:58.340 --> 01:22:02.490
in my community, provide some
protection and some space

01:22:02.490 --> 01:22:05.250
while we build this new thing that I call

01:22:05.250 --> 01:22:09.350
that grows out of my radical
re-imagining of this nation.

01:22:09.350 --> 01:22:11.713
- Hmm, amen.

01:22:11.713 --> 01:22:14.830
I mean, I'm just satisfied
because you responded

01:22:14.830 --> 01:22:18.070
